DefDefinition 39 (Armijo condition)






Definition 39 (Armijo condition) Let \(f : \mathbb{R}^p \to \mathbb{R}\) have first partial derivatives, let \(\mathord{\smash[b]{\underset{\raise.3ex\hbox{$\scriptstyle\sim$}}{x}}\vphantom{x}}\in \mathbb{R}^p\), and let \(\mathord{\smash[b]{\underset{\raise.3ex\hbox{$\scriptstyle\sim$}}{g}}\vphantom{g}} \stackrel{\text{def}}{=}\frac{\partial}{\partial \mathord{\smash[b]{\underset{\raise.3ex\hbox{$\scriptstyle\sim$}}{x}}\vphantom{x}}} f(\mathord{\smash[b]{\underset{\raise.3ex\hbox{$\scriptstyle\sim$}}{x}}\vphantom{x}})\). A step length \(s &gt; 0\) satisfies the Armijo condition [21] with constant \(c \in (0, 1)\) at \(\mathord{\smash[b]{\underset{\raise.3ex\hbox{$\scriptstyle\sim$}}{x}}\vphantom{x}}\) if
\[
f(\mathord{\smash[b]{\underset{\raise.3ex\hbox{$\scriptstyle\sim$}}{x}}\vphantom{x}}- s \mathord{\smash[b]{\underset{\raise.3ex\hbox{$\scriptstyle\sim$}}{g}}\vphantom{g}}) \le f(\mathord{\smash[b]{\underset{\raise.3ex\hbox{$\scriptstyle\sim$}}{x}}\vphantom{x}}) - c\, s\, \mathopen{}\left\lVert\mathord{\smash[b]{\underset{\raise.3ex\hbox{$\scriptstyle\sim$}}{g}}\vphantom{g}}\right\rVert\mathclose{}^2.
\]










ExmExample 55 (The Armijo condition on a parabola)






Example 55 (The Armijo condition on a parabola) Let \(f(x) = x^2\) and \(x = 2\), so \(g = f'(2) = 4\) and \(\mathopen{}\left\lVert g\right\rVert\mathclose{}^2 = 16\). With \(c = 1/4\), the condition on a step length \(s &gt; 0\) is
\[
\begin{aligned}
(2 - 4s)^2 &\le 4 - 4s
&& \text{(} f(2 - 4s) \le f(2) - c\, s\, \mathopen{}\left\lVert g\right\rVert\mathclose{}^2 \text{)}
\\
4 - 16 s + 16 s^2 &\le 4 - 4s
&& \text{(expand the square)}
\\
16 s^2 &\le 12 s
&& \text{(add } 16 s - 4 \text{ to both sides)}
\\
s &\le 3/4.
&& \text{(divide by } 16 s &gt; 0 \text{)}
\end{aligned}
\]
So \(s = 1/2\) satisfies the condition: \(f(0) = 0 \le 4 - 2 = 2\). And \(s = 1\) does not: \(f(-2) = 4 &gt; 4 - 4 = 0\).










DefDefinition 40 (Backtracking line search)






Definition 40 (Backtracking line search) Let \(s_0 &gt; 0\) be an initial step length, \(\beta \in (0, 1)\) a shrink factor, and \(c \in (0, 1)\). Backtracking line search [21] is the line search that chooses \(s^{(t)}\) to be the largest of \(s_0, \beta s_0, \beta^2 s_0, \ldots\) that satisfies the Armijo condition with constant \(c\) at \(\mathord{\smash[b]{\underset{\raise.3ex\hbox{$\scriptstyle\sim$}}{x}}\vphantom{x}}^{(t)}\).










ExmExample 56 (Backtracking on a parabola)






Example 56 (Backtracking on a parabola) For \(f(x) = x^2\) at \(x = 2\) with \(c = 1/4\), the Armijo condition holds exactly when \(s \le 3/4\) (Example 55). With \(s_0 = 1\) and \(\beta = 1/2\), the trial step lengths are \(1, 1/2, 1/4, \ldots\). The first, \(s = 1\), exceeds \(3/4\) and is rejected. The second, \(s = 1/2\), is at most \(3/4\) and is accepted. So backtracking chooses \(s^{(0)} = 1/2\), after two evaluations of \(f\).
